      "degeneracy_caveat": "At the Emb depth ONLY, readout position 1 (the first masked-future token) is bit-identical across windows: its patch-embedding input is (values=0, mask=0) before any recurrence, so the embedding is a pure bias. This is why the HEADLINE geometry is `pos0` (position 0 only, at every depth) and why the `all_positions_from_L1` companion starts at L1: a 2n-row matrix at Emb would be n varying rows plus n copies of one point, which deflates its spectrum and distorts its CKA row relative to every other depth. Neither produced curve contains that matrix. The degeneracy is still measured and reported every run.",
